      "level": 2,
      "content": "Lithosphere vs Asthenosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Asthenosphere is frequently tested as the primary source of magma for volcanic eruptions.",
        "Distinguish clearly between Lithosphere (brittle and solid) and Asthenosphere (plastic and ductile).",
        "The boundary separating the Crust from the Mantle is the Mohorovičić (Moho) Discontinuity."
      ],
      "id": "80v85pn"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The mantle extends from the Mohorovičić discontinuity (Moho) to a depth of 2,900 km.",
        "The Lithosphere consists of the entire crust and the rigid uppermost solid mantle.",
        "The Asthenosphere lies directly below the lithosphere and is composed of ductile, semi-molten rock.",
        "Convection currents originating within the mantle drive the movement of lithospheric tectonic plates."
      ],
      "id": "ilbnlub"
    },
